Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.30,0:00:13.21,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You've had quite a lot \Nof administrative work to do today.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.11,0:00:19.09,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Ah, Grantz. I'll make some tea.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.29,0:00:22.53,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It would be my pleasure \Nto join you, Your Majesty.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.24,0:00:24.74,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Don't be so formal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.74,0:00:26.71,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,We're not king and prime minister here.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.15,0:00:29.42,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I just want to speak as friends right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.91,0:00:33.00,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Understood, Orphanse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.11,0:00:41.43,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Are you troubled over \NPrincess Anisphia again?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.43,0:00:43.90,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I've never {\i1}not{\i0} been troubled over her!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.24,0:00:51.81,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,She's two years older than your Euphyllia,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.81,0:00:55.03,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,and yet that imbecile shows \Nno signs of settling down.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.43,0:00:59.23,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,If she settled down, she wouldn't \Nbe Princess Anisphia anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.74,0:01:03.11,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Her magicology research is \Nshowing results, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.11,0:01:07.46,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,The problem is that she has too much talent \Nfor causing trouble outside her research.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.14,0:01:10.18,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,A parent's work is never done.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.33,0:01:15.38,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It seems that even my son has \Nbecome problematic of late.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.71,0:01:19.85,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You mean the matter with \NBaron Cyan's daughter?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.07,0:01:22.84,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Yes. That fool Algard...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.96,0:01:27.23,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,He has no sense of the standards \Nhe should strive for as future king.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:27.84,0:01:30.31,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,He certainly has been acting quite boldly.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.97,0:01:34.76,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Grantz.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.76,0:01:38.09,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I know the royal family essentially \Nforced this engagement onto you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.09,0:01:41.75,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It's Euphyllia's job to win \Nthe heart of her betrothed.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.27,0:01:45.20,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It should prove to be good experience \Nfor her as the future queen.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.20,0:01:47.50,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,How philosophical of you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.50,0:01:48.01,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,But—
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.56,0:01:50.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.10,0:01:53.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I pray the evening finds you well.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.62,0:01:55.25,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I, Anisphia...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:55.63,0:01:58.46,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,have taken Lady Euphyllia away!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.43,0:03:31.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2}The Magical Revolution
Dialogue: 1,0:03:23.43,0:03:31.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\pos(320,20)\blur2\clip(m 116 13 l 113 58 331 59 328 30 310 58 116 56 120 14 238 18 218 44 192 6 357 14 332 43 331 5 535 5 525 55 473 55 492 25)}The {\c&H7A4AE4&}Mag{\c&HE38B59&}ical {\c&H7A4AE4&}Revol{\c&HE38B59&}ution
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.43,0:03:31.98,Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\fnGeorgia\fad(2025,1)\fs15\pos(320,56)\blur2}of the {\c&H7A4AE4&}Reincarnated Princess {\c&H140900&}and the {\c&HE38B59&}Genius Young Lady
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.93,0:03:36.90,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What is wrong with you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.90,0:03:39.35,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What is {\i1}wrong{\i0} with you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.65,0:03:42.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Please... let me explain my reasoning...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.83,0:03:46.79,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Reasoning?! What excuse is \Nthere for abducting someone?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:46.79,0:03:49.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I was out for a test flight \Nwith my Witch's Broom,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.39,0:03:53.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and I kind of ended up crashing the \Nsoirée at the nobles' academy...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.76,0:03:56.47,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,And there's yet another \Nproblem you've caused!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.47,0:03:58.41,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You fool of a daughter!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.72,0:04:03.34,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And then Al said he was breaking off \Nhis engagement with Lady Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.30,0:04:06.08,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.58,0:04:08.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,He broke off the engagement.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.35,0:04:11.08,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Whose engagement... with whom?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.08,0:04:13.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Al and Lady Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.01,0:04:19.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.69,0:04:22.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I am terribly sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.60,0:04:33.21,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,In the middle of a soirée... \Nin front of all those people...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.85,0:04:35.95,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Of all the times to...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.34,0:04:38.03,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Algard!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.03,0:04:40.50,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What in the world were you thinking?!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.85,0:04:47.02,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.26,0:04:53.97,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Grantz. It seems \Nmy judgment was premature.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.52,0:04:55.52,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Not at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.31,0:04:57.43,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.91,0:05:02.90,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I had heard that you and the prince \Nhad not grown any closer.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.81,0:05:04.98,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.34,0:05:09.42,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It is unfortunate that it ended this way.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.99,0:05:12.88,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I am... very sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.88,0:05:14.83,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,No need to apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.83,0:05:19.28,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,What you need to think about now \Nis what you will do from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.28,0:05:22.25,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,How shall I be punished?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.64,0:05:28.43,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What Euphyllia does from here, eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.63,0:05:31.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's it, Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.35,0:05:33.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's the great idea \NI came to share with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.30,0:05:36.76,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Great idea, you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.92,0:05:39.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Father, Duke Grantz...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:41.16,0:05:44.07,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Please give Lady Euphyllia to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.78,0:05:49.73,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'll do everything in my \Npower to make her happy!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.83,0:05:52.71,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,W...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.71,0:05:55.15,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Wait, wait, wait, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.15,0:05:58.12,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What kind of ridiculous \Njoke are you making?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:58.48,0:06:00.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm being completely serious, Father.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.83,0:06:03.39,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,That's even more frightening!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.39,0:06:05.29,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What, so either way would be wrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:05.29,0:06:07.77,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You're the one who's wrong!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.05,0:06:11.44,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What I'm saying is...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.82,0:06:14.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I want to welcome Lady \NEuphyllia as my assistant!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.24,0:06:18.09,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Me... as your assistant?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.41,0:06:22.43,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,S-So cute...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.43,0:06:26.53,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Those puppy-dog eyes must be \Nsome sort of magic on their own!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.80,0:06:29.45,DefaultItalics,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Her entire existence is OP!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.96,0:06:41.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Th-The problem here is not that \Nthe engagement was annulled,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.22,0:06:43.22,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but that he declared it publicly.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.54,0:06:44.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Correct?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.14,0:06:46.36,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Well, yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:46.36,0:06:50.04,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Since so many people heard it, \Nwe can't take it back.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.04,0:06:54.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you want to arrange an engagement for a \Nlady who's already been spurned by royalty,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.53,0:06:56.40,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,your choice of potential partners is limited.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.66,0:06:58.92,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,And as brilliant as Euphyllia is,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.92,0:07:02.34,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I can't just haphazardly hand \Nher off to some foreign nation.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.98,0:07:05.06,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,After all, Lady Euphyllia...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.06,0:07:07.65,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,is loved by the spirits!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.65,0:07:12.12,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,They say she commands more magical \Nattributes than anyone in history.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.15,0:07:18.14,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And she excels in both etiquette \Nand the martial arts! She's a genius!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.14,0:07:20.55,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,She's the Kingdom of Palettia's treasure!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.61,0:07:23.05,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The best of the best!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.53,0:07:25.88,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And above all...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.46,0:07:28.43,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,She's beautiful {\i1}and{\i0} cute!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.46,0:07:39.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,However, this matter has left a \Nstain on her life as a noble lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.31,0:07:49.57,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,So when you say you want her as your \Nassistant, you mean in magicology?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.71,0:07:53.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The study of magical science that I advocate,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.75,0:07:58.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,"magicology," will, in my opinion, \Nbring about a new of technology.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.08,0:08:00.26,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Well, yes...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.84,0:08:04.78,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It is certainly progressive \Nand full of unknown potential.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.28,0:08:06.36,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Exactly!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.97,0:08:08.95,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,If shared with the public,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.95,0:08:11.88,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,it could greatly impact the entire kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.80,0:08:16.84,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,But you have refrained from \Nannouncing it to the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.84,0:08:19.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I don't really like taking center stage.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.48,0:08:22.07,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I just want to immerse \Nmyself in my research.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.61,0:08:24.51,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I see. In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.99,0:08:26.98,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,you want your achievements \Nin magicology to be...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.95,0:08:31.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Precisely, Duke Grantz!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.54,0:08:35.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Why not have Lady Euphyllia announce \Nthe results of our joint research
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.48,0:08:37.91,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,to restore her damaged reputation?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.91,0:08:39.86,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,M-Me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.48,0:08:41.75,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It could, if nothing else,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.75,0:08:45.09,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,give people something besides the \Nbroken engagement to talk about.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.09,0:08:46.54,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.97,0:08:51.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But... me as your assistant?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.51,0:08:55.48,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,There's plenty that I stand \Nto gain from this deal, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.17,0:08:58.90,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Given the way I am,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.90,0:09:02.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,my reputation is so bad that \NI can't hire a skilled assistant.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.34,0:09:04.84,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But that's...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.21,0:09:08.01,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But you are incredibly talented,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.01,0:09:10.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,and you'd be the perfect choice \Nto promote magicology to the masses.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.81,0:09:15.27,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But wouldn't I be taking \Nall the credit for your work?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.96,0:09:16.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Nah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.42,0:09:19.96,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I'm just doing it out of love!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.87,0:09:23.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,For magicology, you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.08,0:09:23.84,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yep!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:24.41,0:09:26.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It'll change the world we live in.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.62,0:09:29.55,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's new technology, packed \Nwith dreams and romanticism!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.64,0:09:38.17,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,And if possible, I really want\Nyou to fall in love, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.33,0:09:42.02,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Y-You're referring to magicology, right?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.64,0:09:49.02,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Do you remember what you once said to me?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.32,0:09:53.74,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Oh, you mean what she said when \Nshe renounced her right to the throne?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.14,0:09:55.81,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.12,0:10:00.09,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,A long time ago, Princess Anisphia said...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.84,0:10:02.15,Flashback,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Father!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.58,0:10:04.54,Flashback,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Hmm? What is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.78,0:10:07.32,Flashback,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I don't want to marry a man!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.32,0:10:08.55,Flashback,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If I fall in love,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.55,0:10:11.75,Flashback,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I want it to be with a woman!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.15,0:10:13.97,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Are you just making various excuses
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.97,0:10:17.93,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,when all you really want \Nis to make Euphyllia your own?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.61,0:10:25.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Th-That's not... totally wrong, \Nbut... I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:25.51,0:10:27.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I don't want to accidentally \Nget pregnant or anything...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.43,0:10:33.19,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What is {\i1}wrong{\i0} with you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.19,0:10:37.14,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,How dare you speak of such an \Nimportant royal duty in that way?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:37.44,0:10:39.50,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Ow! Ow! Ow!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.50,0:10:43.10,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You're gonna crush your \Nprecious princess's head!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.11,0:10:46.08,DefaultTop,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It would match your twisted \Ndisposition perfectly!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.41,0:10:50.90,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What's the point in passing my genes \Nalong when I can't even use magic?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.04,0:10:51.97,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It's not about having any point!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.97,0:10:55.18,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Do you not understand a father's \Ndesire to see his daughter's child?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.18,0:10:56.71,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,I feel so hopeless, I could cry!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.71,0:11:00.42,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, I'm already crying! \NBawling like a baby!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.42,0:11:02.73,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,You haven't shed a single tear!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.80,0:11:03.86,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Can we just say I understand now?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.53,0:11:08.10,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Is this how a parent and child should be?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.25,0:11:10.56,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.43,0:11:34.54,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, Euphyllia.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.12,0:11:37.09,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,F-Father?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.53,0:11:40.80,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Grantz... bowed his head!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.20,0:11:45.84,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You have worked hard to avoid \Nshaming the Magenta household.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.27,0:11:50.73,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I believed that encouraging you to \Nthat end was my job as your father.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.73,0:11:53.93,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Wh-What are you saying?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.34,0:11:58.24,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I now feel that I may have been mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.36,0:12:04.81,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm who I am today because of \Nthe education you've given me!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.81,0:12:06.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This was all my own fault!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.98,0:12:11.19,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Because I am insufficient as a duke's \Ndaughter, and as a future queen...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.19,0:12:13.47,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm a fool who has besmirched \Nthe name of our—
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.47,0:12:14.72,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,No daughter of mine
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.79,0:12:17.71,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,is a fool.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.88,0:12:22.77,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You lived up to all my expectations.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.77,0:12:24.39,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Too well, in fact.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.00,0:12:28.84,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I've begun to question whether what \N{\i1}you{\i0} wanted played any part in it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.84,0:12:32.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Please stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.84,0:12:36.30,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I really haven't... I'm all right...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.41,0:12:49.01,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I'm sure I haven't been \Na very good father...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.01,0:12:51.22,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,or even a good person.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.61,0:12:54.21,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,You don't need to worry about our family.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.58,0:12:56.83,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,If there's something you want,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.83,0:12:59.55,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I'll make it happen, even if \Nit pits me against the king.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.34,0:13:02.45,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Euphyllia...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.65,0:13:05.91,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Would becoming queen be too much for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.10,0:13:39.42,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Was this really the right thing to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.81,0:13:43.39,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,The princess's villa is an ideal \Nplace for her to lay low.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.39,0:13:47.39,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,And her proposal of joint magicology \Nresearch is worth considering.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.28,0:13:49.35,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Besides...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.85,0:13:51.40,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Besides?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.40,0:13:54.30,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Even if Euphyllia were to be plundered,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.70,0:13:56.53,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,that might not be so bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.53,0:13:57.86,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Grantz!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.86,0:13:59.16,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I was joking.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:59.67,0:14:05.44,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,But there may be meaning in giving \NEuphyllia to Princess Anisphia.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.92,0:14:07.41,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.67,0:14:12.09,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,No law says that there is only one \Npath to succeeding the throne.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.30,0:14:17.33,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,Should a prime minister \Nbe saying that to a king?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.70,0:14:20.71,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,I thought we were supposed to be \Nspeaking as friends right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.33,0:14:24.07,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,Princess Anisphia could be the \Nnext ruler of this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.53,0:14:26.40,Default,Grantz,0,0,0,,It's not such a bad dream to have, is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.35,0:14:30.88,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,That's not a dream I ever want to have.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.88,0:14:32.23,Default,Orphanse,0,0,0,,It's just a nightmare.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.37,0:14:45.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Are you curious about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.43,0:14:49.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's a Thermal Pot,\Nmade with a fire spirit stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.32,0:14:51.37,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Did you invent it?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.37,0:14:54.45,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's set to maintain a given temperature,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.45,0:14:56.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so it can have tea ready in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.91,0:14:59.26,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,It can be used for bathwater, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.26,0:15:02.57,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,I can even wash dishes without \Nhaving the water go cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.53,0:15:06.53,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Please try some.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.53,0:15:10.96,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.39,0:15:13.02,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It is indeed delicious.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.02,0:15:14.42,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Thank you for saying so.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.71,0:15:16.39,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,That's very convenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.39,0:15:19.14,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,It seems as though it could \Nhave many other uses, as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.14,0:15:21.59,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Right? You totally get it!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.59,0:15:24.75,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I guess those who get it... really get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.75,0:15:28.26,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, hey! Since you're here, \Ncome see my workshop!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.69,0:15:29.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.16,0:15:34.62,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you're gonna be my assistant, \Nyou should get a feel for the place first!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.10,0:15:38.80,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,But, Princess Anisphia...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.80,0:15:40.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can call me "Anis."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.76,0:15:42.96,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, and I'll call you "Euphie"!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.48,0:15:45.71,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,We're not strangers anymore, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.71,0:15:48.11,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Er... H-Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.67,0:15:51.92,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,There's no stopping Miss Anis at this point.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.92,0:15:55.78,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Just think of it as being bewitched \Nby a demon and give up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.31,0:15:58.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Let's go, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.30,0:15:59.91,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Anis, wai—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.91,0:16:01.64,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Hang on tight!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.49,0:16:13.15,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Welcome to my workshop!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.12,0:16:18.76,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,There are so many things \NI've never seen before...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.76,0:16:20.57,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You made all these, Princess Anisph—
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.82,0:16:24.33,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I mean, Miss Anis?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.33,0:16:27.04,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,That's right! Praise me, Euphie!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.40,0:16:29.51,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,W-Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:29.51,0:16:32.97,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Please don't spoil Miss Anis too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.51,0:16:39.66,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,The tools themselves are remarkable,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.66,0:16:42.97,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,but I'm shocked that you even had \Nthe idea to use spirit stones.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.97,0:16:47.18,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Oh, well, it's spirits that make \Nthe use of magic possible, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.49,0:16:50.51,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But I can't even sense spirits at all,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.51,0:16:52.39,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,so I can't use magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.01,0:16:54.69,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I had no idea...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.61,0:17:00.27,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,So I had to think of something \Nthat could replace the spirits!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.73,0:17:04.77,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,You truly are amazing, Miss Anis.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.77,0:17:09.76,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I've always taken the existence \Nof magic and spirits for granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.76,0:17:13.58,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I never even considered why \Nthey work the way they do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.58,0:17:16.35,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It's good that you never \Nhad to think about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.35,0:17:18.89,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Since you're compatible with \Nso many different spirits,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.89,0:17:21.56,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,you're OP enough to use \Nany attribute you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.18,0:17:23.52,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,OP?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.25,0:17:25.53,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,The truth is...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.52,0:17:31.47,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I actually envy people who can \Nuse magic. Just a little bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.41,0:17:33.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.94,0:17:36.53,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Because as a princess who can't use magic,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.53,0:17:40.03,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis is the very definition \Nof a useless royal.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.98,0:17:43.71,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Disrespect! Pure disrespect! \NOff with your head!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.71,0:17:45.67,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,How could you say such a thing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.67,0:17:47.42,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,In the Kingdom of Palettia,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.42,0:17:50.35,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,it is said that those who formed \Ncontracts with greater spirits
Dialogue: 0,0:17:50.35,0:17:53.26,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,were the primogenitors of the royal \Nand noble families, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.63,0:17:56.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, but... I know, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.33,0:17:58.60,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Which means the current royalty and nobility
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.60,0:18:01.65,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,are qualified to be as such \Nby the authority of magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.09,0:18:03.57,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis, on the other hand...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.57,0:18:05.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Yeah, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.24,0:18:08.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Magic tools have even more \Npotential than magic itself!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.26,0:18:11.63,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You just don't get it at all, Ilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.00,0:18:15.49,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,If something equivalent to magic could be \Nused to give the people more freedom...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.63,0:18:15.49,DefaultTop,Ilia,0,0,0,,We're not talking about something more \Nthan magic. We're talking about magic.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.49,0:18:19.54,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But you use the Thermal Pot, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.04,0:18:20.20,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,How would the very conservative nobles \Nfeel about their loss of authority?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.20,0:18:25.67,DefaultTop,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What's that supposed to mean?! \NI won't let you use it anymore!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.89,0:18:25.08,DefaultItalics,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,This young woman will prove to be a \Npowerful medicine for this kingdom.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.41,0:18:27.76,Default,Ilia,0,0,0,,Lady Euphyllia?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.13,0:18:29.61,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um, it's nothing...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.19,0:18:33.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Well, it's late, so we're done for today,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.80,0:18:37.81,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but to celebrate your arrival here, \NI'll make you a special magic tool!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:38.47,0:18:40.76,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,For me?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:41.72,0:18:43.33,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Look forward to it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.37,0:18:49.43,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Miss Anis, please stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.43,0:18:52.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,This stuff's hard to take off \Nalone, isn't it? So I'll help!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.68,0:18:53.81,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Wait...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.35,0:19:02.68,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You can borrow some of my pajamas.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.99,0:19:06.05,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Thank you...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.71,0:19:09.68,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Now please go over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.98,0:19:19.63,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Come join me, my lady.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.71,0:19:23.09,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I was just kidding! I won't do anything!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:27.46,0:19:29.00,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Please excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.43,0:19:34.76,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Thanks for coming with me today.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:34.76,0:19:36.30,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I know a lot has happened,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.94,0:19:40.20,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,but I hope you'll see the appeal \Nof magicology and myself soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.18,0:19:48.12,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Yes... You are just as crazy \Nas the rumors say...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.61,0:19:52.08,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And even more mysterious.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.75,0:19:56.81,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Just... what are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:57.50,0:19:59.72,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,What... do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.20,0:20:02.19,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Just from what happened today, I can tell
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.19,0:20:05.79,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,that you are very clever, \Nand that you have big dreams.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.51,0:20:10.90,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I'm sure you're capable of living \Nmore freely than anyone else.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.68,0:20:15.37,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,So why did you help me?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.94,0:20:19.67,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Someone like me, who wasn't \Neven your friend...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.56,0:20:22.66,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I had lots of reasons.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.69,0:20:28.25,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Part of it was that I like you, \Nand part of it was self-interest.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.90,0:20:32.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But the biggest reason was \Nbecause you're perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.34,0:20:34.96,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:35.65,0:20:39.52,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You've always been calm and \Nin control of your emotions.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.54,0:20:42.83,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Even after what happened at the soirée,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.83,0:20:45.24,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,you still tried to remain \Nstrong and righteous.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.19,0:20:49.80,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You really are the perfect duke's daughter.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.80,0:20:53.07,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,I guess that's why I just \Ncouldn't leave you alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.35,0:20:58.06,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,I don't understand. You can't leave \Nme alone because I'm perfect?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.23,0:21:05.67,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If you're someone who can smile on \Nyour own, you can do what you want.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.35,0:21:10.79,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,But it didn't look like you were \Nable to do that as you are now.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.65,0:21:20.59,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,If I really am as free as you say,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:20.59,0:21:25.37,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,then I just can't help reaching out \Nto someone who lacks that freedom.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:27.08,0:21:29.94,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,And that was your only reason for...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.50,0:21:34.93,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,It may seem like a trivial thing, \Nbut it's very important to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.43,0:21:42.60,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Magicians should use their \Nmagic to make others smile.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.69,0:21:48.32,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,You've worked so hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.13,0:21:51.99,Default,Anisphia,0,0,0,,Just rest now, Euphie.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.00,0:21:59.54,Default,Euphyllia,0,0,0,,Goodnight.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.46,0:22:04.97,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Two\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}Acquisition of an Assistant\N for Both Profit and Pleasure
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.97,0:23:39.97,Next Episode Title,Title,0,0,0,,{\pos(320,114)}Episode Three\N\N\N\N\N\N\N\N{\fs25}The Rainbow Magic Sword\N of Longing and Reminiscence
